    <h1>ORUNKA Privacy Policy (summary in English)</h1>
    <p><small>Effective {updated} · Applies to ORUNKA on iPhone and Mac (App Store) and Windows (Steam). The Korean text above is the official version.</small></p>
    <p>ORUNKA is an online game made and run by an individual developer, Sean Son. Sign-in with Apple or Google is required. There are no ads, no analytics and no tracking.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>What we process</strong>: your account ID (uid), sign-in provider and, for Google sign-in, your email (Sign in with Apple does not request your name or email); your game data (character name and look, level, pets, inventory, quests, in-game position, play time, party, when each character slot was last deleted); chat messages and reports; a <strong>gameplay activity log</strong> (time-stamped in-game actions such as connecting and leaving, level-ups, per-minute hunting totals, captures, shop purchases and sales, crafting, quests, trades with the other character and the items, pets and currency exchanged, parties, reports and blocks, character creation and deletion, disconnect reasons, admin edits, penalties, periodic save-summary changes, command counts and timing to spot automation, and your in-game position on each line; if you are muted or suspended, your IP addresses and device types from the last 30 days, up to 5 each — chat text is not included); cheat-suspicion flags with their reasons; connection logs (time, IP address, game version, platform name, sign-in method, game language); per-IP counts of connections that never sign in (not linked to any account); your age and terms confirmation; and emails you send us. We do not collect device IDs, advertising IDs, contacts or precise location, and we do not use IP addresses to find your location.</li>
      <li><strong>Why</strong>: to sign you in, run the game, keep players safe (reports, mutes, suspensions), detect cheating (hacks, macros, bug exploits, real-money trading, funneling from other accounts), handle disputes and appeals, restore lost game data, fix problems and answer support requests. Never for ads or sale.</li>
      <li><strong>Automated processing</strong>: banned words in chat are hidden, disallowed names are refused, and connections that send too many or impossible commands are cut automatically (you can reconnect). A program flags accounts that look like cheating, but a flag alone never leads to a penalty: the developer reviews the records and decides on every mute or suspension.</li>
      <li><strong>Where</strong>: the game server runs on AWS Lightsail in Seoul, Korea. Sign-in is handled by Google Firebase Authentication (USA) and Apple. Support emails to orunka@seanson.com pass through ImprovMX (email forwarding) to Gmail (Google, USA).</li>
      <li><strong>How long</strong>: game saves until you delete your account (dated backups: 14 days; disk snapshots: 7 days); deleted characters: 30 days, so we can restore one on request; chat logs: 30 days; gameplay activity logs and connection logs: <strong>90 days</strong>, also after you delete your account, to check for cheating; suspicion flags: 90 days after the last finding; reports: 1 year, also after you delete your account; terms consent records: while your account exists (the IP address in them is removed after 1 year); warnings and suspensions: 1 year after they end (a permanent ban: while the account exists, then 1 year after deletion); support emails: 1 year after the request is closed. Google keeps sign-in IP addresses for a few weeks and removes deleted accounts from its backups within 180 days.</li>
      <li><strong>Delete your account</strong>: in the game, go to <em>Settings › 계정 (Account) › 계정 지우기 (Delete account)</em> and confirm twice. This deletes your server save and backups (including deleted characters) and your Firebase account, and revokes Sign in with Apple. You can also email us.</li>
      <li><strong>Age</strong>: ORUNKA is for ages 16 and up. If we learn that a child under 16 has signed up, we delete the data.</li>
      <li><strong>Other players</strong> can see your character name, look, level, position and chat in the game. We do not sell or share personal data with third parties, except when the law requires it.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Privacy officer and contact: Sean Son · <a href="mailto:orunka@seanson.com">orunka@seanson.com</a></p>
